<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13595" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dē-versor</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vorsor</span></b> ), ātus,
		1, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. dep.
				n., to be tarrying</i> as a guest, <i>to lodge
				anywhere as a guest</i> (rare but good prose): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cum Athenis apud eum deversarer,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Tusc. 5, 8, 22</span></i>
			; so, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">apud aliquem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Att. 6, 1, 25</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">13, 2, 2</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in domo aliqua,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Verr. 2, 1, 27</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">id. Phil. 2, 27 <i>fin.</i></span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">domi suae deversatum esse,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Verr. 2, 4, 31, § 70</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Liv. 23, 8, 9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">44, 9</span></i>
			<i>fin.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">parum laute,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Verr. 2, 1, 25</span></i>
			.</div>
